"All four V1 blockers are fixed in the code and pass the focused checks, but I have not re-run the full app E2E (`scripts/production/run_e2e_app.mjs`). That run is what proves the fixes on the real 10839000 job, the review-step capture and the K10 orphaned-job capture. It is heavy (engine jobs) and has to run under the shared geometry lock; I updated its assertions so the next run covers these fixes.\n\n**Blockers**\n1. **No part drawn in the real-part 3D view.** An invalid inspection publishes no stage mesh and no scan points, so only bend lines were drawn. The station now draws the finished-part CAD in that case and shows a flag: \"CAD: finished part (scan stage not decoded)\". The Scan and Heatmap buttons are disabled when there are no scan points. In the synthetic check of an invalid inspection, the finished part is drawn as solid CAD (`data-cad-mesh=final`) and fills over 2000 probe pixels.\n2. **Label collisions and wrong highlighted label.** Bend labels are now laid out on screen every frame (new `model/labelLayout.ts`):\n   - no two labels overlap;\n   - a label moved off its anchor gets a leader line back to it;\n   - the selected bend's label is placed first and drawn on top;\n   - no label covers the toolbar, legend or flags.\n\n   A new probe (`frontend/react/scripts/station-label-probe.mjs`) fails if a label's centre hits anything other than itself. The 12-bend fixture (three labels on each anchor) passes it.\n3. **Scrambled PDF header for numeric SKUs.** In `shopfloor_pdf.py` the SKU, recipe id and timestamp after the Hebrew title are now kept as their own left-to-right runs. I reproduced the scrambled order before the fix (\"\u2026 10839000 \u00b7 10839000 \u00b7 Hebrew @v1\"); it now reads \"Hebrew title \u00b7 10839000 \u00b7 10839000@v1\" on every page. A new test in `tests/test_prod_shopfloor_pdf.py` checks this, and the E2E PDF helper has a new `--header-ids` check.\n4. **Review step showing a reset wizard.** This was a screenshot taken before the page loaded, but the wizard did briefly show \"0 of 8 steps done\" and every step as \"To do\". The wizard now shows a loading state until all its data has arrived (`data-loaded`), and the E2E waits for that before the screenshot.\n\n**Polish items done:**\n- \"Releasing\u2026\" now becomes a Released state, and compile warnings read in plain wording with \"\u00b1\".\n- The upload card no longer lingers, and \"Uploading\u2026 100%\" now says the file is processing on the server.\n- Uploaded STEP/PDF files show their real names. This only works in the browser that uploaded them, because the server stores files under generated names; other browsers show \"Folded CAD (STEP)\" or \"Drawing (PDF)\".\n- Flat bend-line chips no longer overlap.\n- The expectations table shows the CAD label next to the recipe label.\n- The 12-bend moves list no longer runs off the panel.\n- The heatmap-unavailable reason is in plain wording, in both languages.\n- The \"?\" on stage chips no longer collides with 10/11/12.\n- Long part names wrap instead of being cut, in both directions.\n- A blank part says \"No bends formed yet\" instead of \"of 0 required checks\".\n- The station flags a running job with no progress for 2 minutes. This is how the K10 orphaned job now shows up.\n- In the PDF, \"Not applicable\" and \"Not yet formed\" have different legend swatches, and an invalid inspection gets one backgauge line instead of 12 empty rows.\n- The E2E now waits for a settled page before each screenshot, starts worst-first from bend 1, and waits for Live before the \"connected\" shot.\n\n**Not done:**\n- The station still shows only the recipe label. The CAD label is not in the result contract, so adding it there needs a contract change.\n- Vendor Setup studio items: clipped hint text and footnotes (they scroll), the CAD badge on the unfolded view, markers moving between modes, and plain label boxes in the wizard's folded 3D view (shared viewer code).\n- The \"Hebrew station he\u2026\" item was cut off in the task text.\n\n**Checks run, all passing:** `tsc`, `npm run lint`, `check-station-layout` (19 steps), `check-station-view-model` (941 assertions), `check-station-fixtures`, `check-onboarding-model` (750), `check-onboarding-ui` (17/17), and pytest `tests/test_prod_shopfloor_pdf.py` plus `tests/test_prod_postprocess_cli.py` (49 passed).\n\nMain files:\n- `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/frontend/react/src/features/station/components/StationViewer.tsx`\n- `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/frontend/react/src/features/station/model/labelLayout.ts` (new)\n- `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/frontend/react/src/features/part-onboarding/pages/OnboardingWizardPage.tsx`\n- `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/domains/production/reporting/shopfloor_pdf.py`\n- `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/scripts/production/run_e2e_app.mjs`"